# Organs that are correctly NOT on a scheduled path: one-shot repairs, audits, CLIs.
# Anything else unreachable is a wiring bug — see invariants.check_wired.
# Adding a name here is a claim that it is meant to be run by hand.
anchors_repair      one-shot: stamps timezones, marks abandoned promises missed
corpus_repair       one-shot: clears canon from rank and the vector index
co_eval             the disposition eval, run by the suite
export_data         member data export
gmail_audit         inbox audit, read-only
regate              re-grade claims in bulk
grade               grading CLI
forget              the forget flow, invoked per request
flib                shared library for the forensic analyzers
email_class         library: the receiving-vs-doing gate
extract_claims      library: email to claims, used by the forensic wave
forensic            the forensic extractor, run against an inbox
synth_calib         library: bounds answer confidence by evidence
whytree             one-shot: builds a why-tree from email
shadow_review       one-shot: grades what the scout proposed
promise_tick        fires requested reminders; LIVE cron */5 — the only proactive class that is never a nag
